{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 65521, "dimension": 8}, "seed": 1146825526, "solved": "failed", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": false, "verify_reason": "evaluated matrix has rank at least 2, exceeding bound 1", "reply": "An affine $9 \\times 9$ matrix $M(x)$ over $\\mathbb{F}_{65521}$ is given, where row 8 is $(0, 0, \\dots, 0, 1)$. For $\\operatorname{rank}(M(x)) \\le 1$, since row 8 is non-zero with only its last entry non-zero and every other row has 0 in column 8, every other row must be $0 \\cdot \\text{row } 8 = \\mathbf{0}$.\n\nThus, all entries $M(x)_{i,j} = 0$ for $0 \\le i, j \\le 7$. The 64 variables partition into 8 disjoint sets of 8 variables, one set per column. Each column yields an independent linear system of the form:\n$$A_j v_j + c_j = 0 \\pmod{65521}$$\nwhere each $A_j$ is an $8 \\times 8$ Hadamard matrix ($A_j^T A_j = 8 I_8$). The unique solution for each column vector of variables is:\n$$v_j = -A_j^{-1} c_j = -\\frac{1}{8} A_j^T c_j \\pmod{65521}$$\n\nSolving each system gives the values for all 64 variables $x_0, \\dots, x_{63}$, which are pairwise distinct.\n\n<answer>[15333, 63175, 48929, 40340, 59594, 29462, 44584, 45986, 49022, 8005, 63122, 62375, 26347, 37722, 41527, 4440, 44858, 61172, 18210, 34337, 9839, 28805, 49809, 48949, 6997, 28521, 16553, 27361, 48906, 42998, 8878, 13943, 61619, 5857, 16674, 34095, 23153, 55882, 52546, 3531, 59958, 18892, 12555, 55597, 40060, 6294, 8599, 61218, 17313, 61243, 62188, 50732, 33447, 47550, 48980, 48420, 60726, 51101, 58017, 59134, 28846, 13307, 14567, 31100]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 145.13, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "hard", "escalation_round": 2}
